DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The group service module for PAM accepts or rejects users based on their
     membership in a particular file group.  ppaamm__ggrroouupp provides functionality
     for two PAM categories: authentication and account management.  In terms
     of the module-type parameter, they are the ``auth'' and ``account'' fea‐
     tures.

     The following options may be passed to the ppaamm__ggrroouupp module:

     ddeennyy       Reverse the meaning of the test, i.e., reject the applicant if
                and only if he or she is a member of the specified group.
                This can be useful to exclude certain groups of users from
                certain services.

     ffaaiill__ssaaffee  If the specified group does not exist, or has no members, act
                as if it does exist and the applicant is a member.

     ggrroouupp=_g_r_o_u_p_n_a_m_e
                Specify the name of the group to check.  The default is
                “wheel”.

     lluusseerr      Accept or reject based on the target user's group membership.

     rroooott__oonnllyy  Skip this module entirely if the target account is not the su‐
                peruser account.

     rruusseerr      Accept or reject based on the supplicant's group membership.
                This is the default.

     Note that the lluusseerr and rruusseerr options are mutually exclusive, and that
     ppaamm__ggrroouupp will fail if both are specified.

